    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Gunnar Henderson** (70.40) anchoring the lineup, representing our highest efficiency plays. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits immensely from a favorable matchup against Burnes, whose 5.41 xERA suggests he will struggle against our middle-infield core, while **Gunnar Henderson** thrives despite a tough opposing arm thanks to a massive 16% park adjustment and a strong #3 order placement. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (70.07) earns a spot as a priority start; while his raw base is moderate, his elite speed profile and positive platoon dynamic against Alcantara make him a critical asset in our hunt for the scarce stolen base category. **Heliot Ramos** (67.50) is also a strong play, riding the wave of that same favorable Burnes matchup to elevate his score well into our recommended tier.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Josh Jung** (43.41), who hovered near the threshold of viability but ultimately lacked the high-end ceiling required to displace the current starters. His matchup against Miles\u2014a quality arm with a 3.24 xERA\u2014neutered his upside, leading us to favor the offensive environments surrounding **Coby Mayo** and **Wade Meckler** instead. We are exercising caution with **Henry Bolte** (41.35), whose score is suppressed by a difficult clash with Williams; he remains in the lineup purely to maintain our 5x5 coverage, but he carries the highest volatility risk of our starters today. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the top-tier arms we are facing. Both **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.39) and **Coby Mayo** (44.06) are drawing Misiorowski and deGrom respectively, two pitchers with elite xERA marks under 3.00. While their scores are bolstered by order placement and park factors, these are \"survive and advance\" scenarios for these bats. Conversely, **Nasim Nunez** (51.79) provides necessary stability at 2B, and while his order placement is suboptimal, his versatility keeps him ahead of our bench alternatives. As we navigate the remainder of the season, maintaining this level of daily efficiency is vital to closing the gap in our Roto standings.",
